# The kind lab on Kubara v0.16.0, recorded from scratch on 2026-09-30 with cub
# kubara built from the kubara-v0.16-catalog-upgrade branch (0.3.0-dev), then a
# catalog upgrade taken through ConfigHub.
#
# up.sh built the platform with Kubara v0.16.0 and its default catalogs,
# bootstrap and general 3.0.0, on kind v0.31.0 with Kubernetes v1.35.0, on
# clusters named klab16-hub and klab16-spoke (KIND=klab16). Kubara's bootstrap
# installed Argo CD 3.5.2 on the hub. run.sh and upgrade.sh ran against a hosted
# ConfigHub organization with cub v0.6.8 and PREFIX=klab-0930-v16.
#
# up.sh took 7 minutes, run.sh 22 and upgrade.sh 12. The lab directory is shown
# as ./kubara-lab. On kind, cert-manager is Degraded (Let's Encrypt refuses the
# example.com contact), traefik is Progressing (no load balancer), and the
# hub's argocd Application waits for an Ingress address.
#
# What to look for:
# - Kubara v0.16.0 needed no change to cub kubara. Every section of run.sh
#   passed, as on v0.15.0. up.sh's first attempt stopped at step 4: kubectl
#   could not attach to the pod that checks the Git server ("no running task
#   found"). up.sh now tries that check three times; this log is its second run.
# - upgrade.sh section 1: bootstrap 5.0.1 and general 5.1.0 move argo-cd to
#   chart 10.9.2 (Argo CD v3.5.3), cert-manager to 1.21.2 and traefik to chart
#   41.6.0 (v3.7.13). metrics-server and homer-dashboard do not change.
# - Section 3: apply.sh proposes one change order per base whose render changed
#   (argo-cd, bootstrap-crds, cert-manager, traefik), and none for the others.
#   The argo-cd base keeps the routing handover gave it: 5 ApplicationSets
#   still read ConfigHub.
# - Sections 4 and 5: traefik v3.7.13 reaches dev while prod stays on v3.7.12,
#   then prod after its own approval.
#
# Section 6 of upgrade.sh, as it stood for this run, released the argo-cd
# change to dev. It did not land, and the script stopped (the end of this log).
# The hub's argocd Application had a sync from handover still Running, waiting
# for an Ingress address kind never gives, and Argo CD starts no new sync while
# one runs. After that sync was stopped, Argo CD did not sync on its own
# ("Skipping auto-sync: failed previous sync attempt"), and a sync started by
# hand also waited on the Ingress, with argocd-server still on v3.5.2. Section 6
# is now left out of upgrade.sh, and the argo-cd change order waits.
#
# An earlier attempt of upgrade.sh, the same day on fresh Spaces, found that
# `cub unit create --allow-exists`, which apply.sh used for each base, merges a
# new file into a base that exists, with no change order. The bases took the
# new catalog silently. apply.sh now creates a base only when it is missing, and
# proposes Kubara's new render through a change order instead.

######## KIND=klab16 bash examples/kind-lab/up.sh   (kubara v0.16.0 on the PATH)


